1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Hinatsu!

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
I'll see you next time.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:29,980
I'll see you next time.

4
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:59,980
I'll see you next time.

5
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:29,980
I'll see you next time.

6
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
She always knew exactly what I was doing, so I was unable to contact you.

7
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:42,560
Lord Tengen, please leave this place and don't trouble yourself with me.

8
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:46,500
You heard that sound just now. I know you did.

9
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,840
That demon is on a rampage.

10
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:53,840
Can you promise me that you'll be okay?

11
00:02:55,120 --> 00:03:00,160
I promise. I am so sorry that I couldn't be more helpful to you.

12
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:04,000
You've done everything that you possibly could.

13
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:09,500
Once the antidote kicks in, leave Yoshiwara.

14
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:11,500
Understood.

15
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,500
Yes.

16
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:25,120
The battle's already begun.

17
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:26,740
Where is it?

18
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:28,840
Search for its presence.

19
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:36,040
It's here.

20
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:37,080
Underground.

21
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:41,260
I can hear the sound of someone fighting.

22
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:45,080
If I focus on the reverberations...

23
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:49,080
Then I can locate them.

24
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,020
Sound breathing.

25
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:54,900
First form.

26
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:56,160
Roar!

27
00:03:56,160 --> 00:04:02,100
That infernal racket is giving me a headache.

28
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,720
What is all that noise?

29
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:05,080
What is it you're up to?

30
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:08,420
It sounds like it's coming from the Ogimoto house.

31
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:11,080
That damn Hinatsuru.

32
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:14,060
Exactly how many of you are there?

33
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:15,220
Four, perhaps?

34
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:16,540
Who knows?

35
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:19,040
Well then, if you were to tell me the truth,

36
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,740
I might be willing to spare your worthless life.

37
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:25,000
We only clashed for maybe an instant at most.

38
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:26,900
But look at your sword.

39
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:28,420
It's already chipped.

40
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,020
The swordsmith who made it must have been a real amateur.

41
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:36,440
You're wrong!

42
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:38,720
The person who forged this is amazing!

43
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:40,880
And he's a brilliant swordsmith!

44
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:41,900
Oh really?

45
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:44,340
How did it get chipped then, you moron?

46
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,700
Over there now too?

47
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:49,880
Such an obnoxious racket.

48
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:52,300
I'm growing tired of it.

49
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:54,600
So I'm putting an end to you now.

50
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,640
The blade suffers when its wielder is inadequate.

51
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:00,780
It's my fault.

52
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:03,780
Despite training my hardest, I still...

53
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:09,080
I still can't handle the water breathing technique yet.

54
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:15,540
And the truth is, my body's just not suited for it.

55
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:21,940
If I keep using water breathing, I'll never be like Mr. Urokodaki or Mr. Tomioka.

56
00:05:22,620 --> 00:05:27,620
For me, using Hinokami Kagura to strike my enemies has always been more effective.

57
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:30,620
I feel more in tune with it.

58
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:31,620
I feel more in tune with it.

59
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:34,620
And yet...

60
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:42,160
Hey moron, would it kill you to hold back a little?

61
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:46,280
What's the point if you don't give it your all?

62
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,600
Hinokami Kagura!

63
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,980
Flame dance!

64
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:54,180
Clear blue!

65
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:58,760
Tanjiro!

66
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:01,120
Hey, what happened?

67
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:01,840
Are you okay?

68
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,080
Hey, are you hungry?

69
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:03,940
Shut up!

70
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:09,200
Because of its sheer force, I couldn't unleash multiple strikes.

71
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,620
But it's different now.

72
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:15,520
I should be able to do it.

73
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:16,900
No.

74
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,600
I can't do it.

75
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,380
That is what I've been training for.

76
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,300
Don't go down in defeat.

77
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:24,320
Burn!

78
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:25,660
Burn!

79
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:26,920
Burn!

80
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,420
Set your heart ablaze!

81
00:06:29,420 --> 00:06:32,760
Hinokami Kagura!

82
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:36,520
Raging Sun!

83
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:40,620
His swordsmanship style changed.

84
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,260
It's sharper than before.

85
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:46,400
What is that sound he's emitting?

86
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:48,060
It's unpleasant as hell.

87
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:49,740
Is it his breathing?

88
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,800
Flame dance!

89
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:57,260
She dodged the first one, but this move is a two-hit strike.

90
00:06:57,740 --> 00:06:59,160
That was underwhelming.

91
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:00,420
But...

92
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:01,560
So typical!

93
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:06,180
He's gone?

94
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:09,100
Hinokami Kagura!

95
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:10,340
Fake rainbow!

96
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:14,120
There it is!

97
00:07:14,380 --> 00:07:15,440
The opening thread!

98
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:17,040
I can do this!

99
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,020
Hinokami Kagura!

100
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:20,200
Firewheel!

101
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,220
Far too slow.

102
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,840
You're making me yawn.

103
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:31,760
I have to use the defensive falling technique!

104
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:46,040
This is the drawback of using Hinokami Kagura.

105
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:49,840
All the built-up fatigue is causing my muscles to cramp.

106
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,240
Still alive over there?

107
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:54,960
Calm down.

108
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:56,500
Get your breathing under control.

109
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:58,500
And recover!

110
00:07:58,500 --> 00:07:58,960
And recover!

111
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:00,900
Quickly!

112
00:08:01,460 --> 00:08:02,400
Recovery breathing!

113
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:16,220
This belt is no different than a powerful blade.

114
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,780
Even if I glimpse an opening thread, it vanishes instantly!

115
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:22,600
My attacks are too slow!

116
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,120
My body temperature!

117
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:27,940
If I'm gonna win, I need to raise my body temperature!

118
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:29,400
Are you sure?

119
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:31,280
I think I should tell Lady Shinobu.

120
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:34,280
Your body temperature still hasn't gone down yet.

121
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:35,180
Please don't!

122
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:35,980
I'm begging you!

123
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:37,260
Keep it between us!

124
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:38,540
Really, I'm fine now!

125
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,300
There's no use in telling her!

126
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:41,780
Yes, but still...

127
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:43,560
Look, I'm fine, see?

128
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:44,760
Never felt better!

129
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:46,000
Just a little warm!

130
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,800
Being a little warm is okay, but look at this!

131
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:50,640
It says 100 degrees!

132
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,620
It was that high yesterday and the day before, too!

133
00:08:54,020 --> 00:08:55,380
That's not good!

134
00:08:57,780 --> 00:09:00,420
If you have a fever that won't go down,

135
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:02,900
that means something's wrong with your body, Tanjiro!

136
00:09:03,780 --> 00:09:08,220
I'm not skilled enough to know what to do about something like this,

137
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,000
but Lady Shinobu would!

138
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:16,040
The thing is,

139
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:17,740
when I have a fever,

140
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:19,980
I'm actually at the top of my game!

141
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:23,320
I can use multiple Hino Kami Kagura strikes,

142
00:09:23,740 --> 00:09:25,740
and I might become even stronger with it!

143
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:27,480
Please, Kiyo,

144
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:30,600
can't you wait just a little longer before telling Miss Shinobu?

145
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:33,060
Just a little bit longer!

146
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:34,540
I'm begging you!

147
00:09:37,540 --> 00:09:38,780
Very well, then.

148
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,380
But only just a little longer!

149
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:48,180
It's working.

150
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:50,520
I can feel my body temperature rising.

151
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:52,060
I can do this.

152
00:09:52,420 --> 00:09:53,940
I can take on an upper-ranked demon!

153
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:57,560
He's a pesky one.

154
00:09:57,900 --> 00:09:59,140
More than I thought he'd be.

155
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:00,740
How entertaining.

156
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:02,320
Focus!

157
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:05,000
Hino Kami Kagura's effective against her!

158
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:08,840
But it's not enough to just be effective!

159
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:11,480
If I want to win,

160
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:14,000
I'm going to have to use every ounce of my power!

161
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,980
And I have to win!

162
00:10:17,020 --> 00:10:18,520
To protect the innocent!

163
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:21,280
To protect my friends!

164
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:26,220
Never again will I allow chaos like that to unfold!

165
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:30,080
Never again will I let anyone suffer the way that we did!

166
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:33,400
No one should have to bear that kind of grief!

167
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:44,000
The way you sweat like a pig is truly repulsive!

168
00:10:44,000 --> 00:11:02,620
What's all that screaming about?

169
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:03,700
It's a monster!

170
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:04,800
A monster!

171
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,980
There's no time to fool around!

172
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,020
Get ready for work!

173
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:12,780
Who cares about work when there's a monster board going around destroying all the ceilings and floors?

174
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:13,400
What?

175
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:16,220
Are you sure you got enough sleep last night?

176
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,040
Come see!

177
00:11:17,100 --> 00:11:17,660
I'll show you!

178
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:18,080
Ah!

179
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,320
Ah!

180
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:24,680
Ah!

181
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:26,300
Ah!

182
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:29,720
Now I'm really feeling that demon's present!

183
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:30,980
Ah!

184
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:31,360
Ah!

185
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:34,280
Isn't he here?

186
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:35,300
Ah!

187
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:40,200
This must be it!

188
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:42,700
The hole leading straight to the demon's lair!

189
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:44,520
Get ready to die, bastard!

190
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,940
So I can only get my head inside, huh?

191
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:57,360
That might have stopped others, but it's not going to stop Lordy Nose Day!

192
00:11:58,540 --> 00:12:02,300
After all, I'm a man who can dislocate all his joints!

193
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:07,200
In other words, as long as my head spits, I can go anyway!

194
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:14,820
Get ready, demon, cause I'm coming through!

195
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:16,920
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

196
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:18,380
Watch this!

197
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:20,720
There's no one in sight to this damn thing!

198
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,260
Oh, it's here!

199
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:24,380
I can tell there's a demon here!

200
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:27,440
I can tell there's a demon here!

201
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,040
I can tell there's a demon here!

202
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:28,580
I can tell there's a demon here!

203
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:34,260
What the hell?

204
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:48,240
Some kind of cloth with a human pattern?

205
00:12:49,160 --> 00:12:50,980
What is this?

206
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:54,220
No, that's not just a pattern.

207
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:56,300
Those are living humans.

208
00:12:56,300 --> 00:13:01,420
So this demon is able to trap humans inside of a woman's belt, huh?

209
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:09,280
That it takes them whenever it wants and devours them?

210
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:11,860
Pretty brutal if you ask me.

211
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:18,420
What's he doing here?

212
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:20,900
That's a question I should be asking you.

213
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:24,720
How would you like it if someone started messing with your food?

214
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:28,140
Dirty man, you reek of filth.

215
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:32,460
Disgusting, repulsive, you damn stink bug!

216
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:34,320
Look who's talking, you worm!

217
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:35,080
Gross!

218
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:38,220
You dare insult me, stink bug!

219
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:42,540
Riggle, wiggle, wiggle, wiggle!

220
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:46,380
You are really grossing me out, worm belt!

221
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:47,660
Ha ha ha!

222
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,520
Look how sluggish you are!

223
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:53,220
You got greedy and swallowed up too many humans!

224
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:56,260
There's no way an attack from an overweight worm!

225
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:59,800
Can ever hook to land a lordy nose day!

226
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,420
So lose some weight!

227
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,600
And don't come back to your head!

228
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:09,140
Dammit, he managed to slice me without touching the humans!

229
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:13,340
After I went to the trouble of storing all that fresh food, too!

230
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:20,060
His intuition appears to be razor sharp, and his ability to detect murderous intent is exceptional.

231
00:14:20,060 --> 00:14:25,680
It's so precise that he could receive attacks from any direction and dodge them effortlessly.

232
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:30,920
I never anticipated a Demon Slayer swordsman would infiltrate our food supply!

233
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:32,860
What should I do?

234
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:35,700
Capture him alive!

235
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:41,520
He's the brat who got in my way when I captured Makio earlier.

236
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:43,740
He was beautiful.

237
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:49,980
You can kill all of the humans you have stored, but save the ten most beautiful ones from me.

238
00:14:50,980 --> 00:14:54,840
Though it might prove harder to capture them alive than to merely kill them.

239
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:59,620
If you devour some of the uglier ones, that should make things easier.

240
00:14:59,620 --> 00:15:01,620
Rrrrraaargh!

241
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:07,260
I can't slash it when it's flapping like that!

242
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:19,020
Let's see you deal with beast-breathing six fang.

243
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,640
Palisade bite!

244
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:25,700
Slashing me is useless when I'm not even the main body, you fool!

245
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:31,700
Never mind. The humans you saved are looking awfully vulnerable, don't you think?

246
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:38,960
Not to mention I can recover from any damage you manage to inflict.

247
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:45,740
No crap! I forgot! I've gotta fight it while protecting those humans, don't I?

248
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:48,140
Dammit! I can't keep up!

249
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:50,020
Annoying Worm Belt!

250
00:15:50,020 --> 00:15:56,100
I gotta hand it to you, Worm Belt's a pretty good name.

251
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:58,160
Yeah, it's perfect for something so gross!

252
00:15:58,300 --> 00:15:59,780
And I'm so gonna tell on you!

253
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:02,300
Just wait until Lord Tengen finds out!

254
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:08,420
We're gonna give you a hand with this freak, so fight the good fight, my four-headed friend!

255
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:11,600
Who the heck are you two?

256
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:13,220
Most of us are Usly's wives!

257
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:15,960
I'm trying my best here, but I'm not much of a fighter!

258
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:19,440
Please don't expect much from me!

259
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:21,140
Zuma!

260
00:16:21,660 --> 00:16:23,720
This is no time to be acting like a witch!

261
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:26,180
I will mock you! I can't help it!

262
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:28,640
You know I'm a good-for-nothing, especially when it comes to fighting!

263
00:16:29,060 --> 00:16:29,880
I got captured!

264
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:33,000
You can't expect me to protect everyone else who got captured!

265
00:16:33,180 --> 00:16:36,040
It's impossible! I'll be the one who gets killed first, probably!

266
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:39,400
It's a shame your friends don't think more like you.

267
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:42,740
Now, which of you should I eat first?

268
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:45,840
Damn that thing! It's not the main body!

269
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:48,000
If that's true, I'm screwed!

270
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,220
Dude, this battle's never gonna end!

271
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:52,120
Thunder Breathing.

272
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:53,980
First form.

273
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:56,200
Thunderclap and flash.

274
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:57,700
Six-fold!

275
00:16:57,700 --> 00:17:15,740
Maybe you should stay asleep like this the whole time.

276
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:17,540
Muscle!

277
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:18,620
Muscle!

278
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:20,940
Is he Demon Slayer, Korra?

279
00:17:21,300 --> 00:17:23,600
If he is, then why does he dress like a total idiot?

280
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,080
Yeah! Good question!

281
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:27,960
Such blinding speed.

282
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:29,500
Who is that boy?

283
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:31,880
Regardless, he's not alone.

284
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:34,240
I'm sure I heard two sounds.

285
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:38,460
Like overlapping thunderbolts creating two sounds at once.

286
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:40,560
One was that boy.

287
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:43,740
And the other one came from above.

288
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:53,680
The wind?

289
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:55,100
How is that possible?

290
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:59,640
What's powerful enough to create a hole that reaches this step?

291
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:01,720
What the hell?

292
00:18:03,260 --> 00:18:04,640
This presence...

293
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:08,060
Someone's here.

294
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,200
I know it.

295
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:20,080
Such strength!

296
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,340
Ahashi-ro!

297
00:18:22,340 --> 00:18:38,520
Lord Tengen.

298
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:43,420
Makio.

299
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:44,360
Suma.

300
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:47,020
Sorry I took so long.

301
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:51,320
You both look as flashy as ever.

302
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:59,120
You know, it wasn't like this before.

303
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:04,840
The thought of dying never used to bother me, since that's how I was trained.

304
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:13,880
Furthermore, since I was a kunoichi, I could never hope to match a male shinobi in terms of raw strength.

305
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:18,800
So risking my life for a mission was the least I could do to make up for it.

306
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:26,500
You three are only to think about your own lives from here on out.

307
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:30,820
Above all else, your top priority is to come back alive.

308
00:19:31,540 --> 00:19:33,540
Life over accomplishing your mission.

309
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:37,840
I understand that conflicts with your occupation, but it doesn't matter.

310
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:39,200
I'm allowing it.

311
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:43,400
You are to live your lives in the following flashy order.

312
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:48,860
First, prioritize your own lives.

313
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:50,980
Then second, law-abiding citizens.

314
00:19:51,420 --> 00:19:53,140
And finally, my own.

315
00:19:54,180 --> 00:19:59,660
As the Demon Slayer swordsman, it goes without saying I'll protect the public leading their unflashy lives.

316
00:19:59,660 --> 00:20:04,040
But if I'm being completely honest, I'll always prioritize you three.

317
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:05,600
So don't you die on me.

318
00:20:07,300 --> 00:20:08,980
You can't be serious right now.

319
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:16,040
If you put your own life first before the mission, can you really hope to accomplish anything significant?

320
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:18,960
Don't worry.

321
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:23,200
If Lord Tengen says it's fine, then I trust him.

322
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:28,960
Putting your own life before others or a mission doesn't sound like a bad way to live at all.

323
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:30,340
Don't you think?

324
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:35,400
As long as you don't despise yourself for it, it's totally fine.

325
00:20:36,260 --> 00:20:36,640
You know?

326
00:20:41,860 --> 00:20:42,600
You're right.

327
00:20:42,600 --> 00:21:03,160
You've been doing some flashy work here.

328
00:21:05,280 --> 00:21:06,540
You're my wives.

329
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:08,140
I'd expect nothing less.

330
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:29,280
From here on out, things are gonna get real flashy.

331
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:59,260
You're my wife.

332
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:29,260
You're my wife.

333
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:59,260
You're my wife.

334
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:03,200
It's a joke, right?

335
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:05,660
The Saunashiro can't possibly have three wives.

336
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:07,800
Well, why don't you try for that, Zenitsu?

337
00:23:08,020 --> 00:23:08,660
What? Really?

338
00:23:09,220 --> 00:23:11,900
Okay, well, then there's Yoshiko, Sanai, and then there's Osa...

339
00:23:11,900 --> 00:23:13,440
I guess I have to let Nezuko know.

340
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:14,660
Wait! Taichiro, no!

341
00:23:15,080 --> 00:23:17,360
Now it's time for a Taisho-era secret.

342
00:23:18,140 --> 00:23:20,440
Mr. Uzui's whole family practices polygamy,

343
00:23:20,780 --> 00:23:22,340
and I hear that when you turn 15,

344
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:25,460
the head of the family picks out three wives that are sure to be a fit.

345
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:29,000
But they say that Miss Suma actually stepped forward and offered herself.

346
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:31,360
Then maybe I should become a Shinobi, too.

347
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:34,060
Then you'll be starting Shinobi training today, right?

348
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:34,640
Huh?

349
00:23:36,700 --> 00:23:39,260
Next episode six, Layered Memories.

